[{"sha":"f18cc4d4cdfc6e14506c5eb1047bb4daf1462e0c","node_id":"C_kwDOT0qK59oAKGYxOGNjNGQ0Y2RmYzZlMTQ1MDZjNWViMTA0N2JiNGRhZjE0NjJlMGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"£","email":"kenpachi.eth@outlook.com","date":"2026-08-13T08:16:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"£","email":"kenpachi.eth@outlook.com","date":"2026-08-13T08:16:51Z"},"message":"Migrate TEE off local Docker to AWS, pause old teeId, update docs\n\nThe dispute-path TEE stack (extension-tee + ext-proxy + redis) now runs on a\ndedicated AWS instance instead of local Docker Desktop behind a rotating\ntrycloudflare.com quick tunnel -- the tunnel had already died and needed\nmanual recovery twice this session. Fully live, no cost:\n\n- Resized the instance (t3.micro -> t3.small) for headroom after confirming\n  the old size had ~268MB RAM free with existing infra already running.\n- Elastic IP for a permanent public address, Caddy + Let's Encrypt for real\n  HTTPS via sslip.io's free wildcard DNS -- no Cloudflare account or paid\n  domain needed in the end.\n- New teeId registered and reached PRODUCTION; old local teeId paused\n  on-chain so instruction routing only ever reaches the AWS one.\n- Re-ran the evidence-submission round trip against the new TEE and got an\n  identical real signed verdict, confirming parity with the original local\n  run.\n\nTASK2.md and PHASE3.md updated with the current live identifiers -- original\nhistorical tx hashes and narratives left intact.","tree":{"sha":"2d9f52ae1dacbdaff1fcfe03e164702fdb3e9a22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/danielamodu/Warden/git/trees/2d9f52ae1dacbdaff1fcfe03e164702fdb3e9a22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/danielamodu/Warden/git/commits/f18cc4d4cdfc6e14506c5eb1047bb4daf1462e0c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/danielamodu/Warden/commits/f18cc4d4cdfc6e14506c5eb1047bb4daf1462e0c","html_url":"https://github.com/danielamodu/Warden/com